Package: templaros-nm-tray
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, network-manager
Provides: nm-tray
Conflicts: nm-tray
Replaces: nm-tray
Description: network control for the TemplarOS Home Field
 A Qt6 NetworkManager front end, forked from palinek/nm-tray so that it can be
 driven without a system tray: TemplarOS has no taskbar to host an applet, so the
 Home Field's network control launches this with --popup and an already-running
 instance takes the request over the session bus instead of duplicating itself.
 .
 The package installs nm-tray.desktop, which is the name the shell resolves when
 no application declares org.templaros.NetworkTray
 (shell/templar-shell/src/surface/app.rs).
